IMPORT prelude

-- Straits Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928 (Singapore) -- Parliament's approval of the 1927 Agreement
-- (s 1) and the Agreement in the Schedule: the boundary between the territorial waters of the Settlement of Singapore and those of
-- Johore (Article I), the ceded waters within three nautical miles of the Johore mainland (Article II), the retrocession of islets
-- (Article III) and the Agreement having no force until approved (Article IV).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SSJTWAA1928.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries no amendment
-- annotations. The Legislative History (not part of the Act) lists only the original Act, 18 & 19 Geo. V, c. 23 (commencement
-- 3 August 1928), noting it was declared by the Application of English Law Act 1993 to apply or continue to apply in Singapore, and
-- the 1985 Revised Edition (operation 30 March 1987). No amending Act is listed.
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS in the deposit is out of step by one line (it numbers "1." blank and "2. Approval of Agreement"); the
-- BODY's numbering (s 1 approval, s 2 short title) is followed here.
-- The map annexed to the Agreement ("delineated in red") is not in the deposit.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0255 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The honest answer is: nothing directly. The Act creates no right, duty, offence, penalty or deadline for any
-- person. What it decides is WHOSE territorial waters a stretch of sea is, and who holds certain islets -- which is the question a
-- fisherman, a boat operator or anyone in Johore Strait would be asking. That is what is encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the recitals and the 1824 Treaty itself (which waters were ceded is taken as a given fact); the actual geography (the
-- position of the deep-water channel, the low water mark, the 3-mile limits) -- each is an input fact, not computed; the map; the
-- signatures and witnesses; s 2 (short title); and what happened to the Settlement's waters after 1928 (independence, later treaties
-- and the Territorial Waters law of today are not in this deposit and are not considered).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill (not loadable in this session, so the conventions
-- of the finished naive rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Straits Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928 -- nouns`

DECLARE `Waters of` IS ONE OF
    `the Settlement of Singapore`
    `the State and Territory of Johore`
    `not decided by the Agreement`

-- A place at sea, described by the facts the Agreement turns on. Every field is a finding of geography the Agreement does not make.
DECLARE Place HAS
    `in Johore Strait or at its entrances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the Johore mainland side of the boundary line` IS A BOOLEAN
    `among the waters ceded by the 1824 Treaty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within three nautical miles of the Johore mainland from low water mark` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Island IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `Pulau Ubin`
    `Pulau Tekong Kechil`
    `Pulau Tekong Besar`
    `Pulau Merambong`
    `Johore Shoal`

DECLARE `Boundary line` IS ONE OF
    `the centre of the deep-water channel`
    `midway between the two portions`

DECLARE Entrance IS ONE OF
    `the Western entrance`
    `the Eastern entrance`

DECLARE `Seaward end` IS ONE OF
    `the 3-mile limit from the low water mark of the South Coast of Pulau Merambong`
    `the 3-mile limit from the low water mark of the Johore mainland, bearing 192 degrees from Tanjong Sitapa`

DECLARE `Cause of conflict` IS ONE OF
    `alterations in the channels`
    `some other cause`

DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the text of the Agreement`
    `the annexed map`

§§ `s 1 and Article IV -- approval and force`

-- Preamble: "it is provided by the said Agreement that it shall remain without force or effect until it has received the approval of
-- Parliament". Article IV: "This Agreement shall remain without force or effect until it has received the approval of the British
-- Parliament." s 1: "The approval of Parliament is hereby given to the said Agreement."
-- The Act itself is that approval; the input lets the encoding show what Article IV does without it.
GIVEN `Parliament has approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agreement has force or effect` IF `Parliament has approved it`

§§ `Article I -- the boundary in Johore Strait`

-- Article I: the boundary "shall, except as hereafter specified in this Article, be an imaginary line following the centre of the
-- deep-water channel in Johore Strait, between the mainland of the State and Territory of Johore on the one side and the Northern Shores
-- of the Islands of Singapore, Pulau Ubin, Pulau Tekong Kechil, and Pulau Tekong Besar on the other side. Where, if at all, the channel
-- divides into two portions of equal depth running side by side, the boundary shall run midway between these two portions."
GIVEN `the channel divides into two portions of equal depth running side by side` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Boundary line`
DECIDE `the boundary line in the Strait` IS
    IF `the channel divides into two portions of equal depth running side by side`
    THEN `midway between the two portions`
    ELSE `the centre of the deep-water channel`

GIVEN `the island` IS AN Island
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its Northern Shore faces the boundary on the Singapore side` IF
    CONSIDER `the island`
    WHEN `Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pulau Ubin` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pulau Tekong Kechil` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pulau Tekong Besar` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "At the Western entrance of Johore Strait, the boundary, after passing through the centre of the deep-water channel Eastward of Pulau
-- Merambong, shall proceed seaward, in the general direction of the axis of this channel produced, until it intersects the 3-mile limit
-- drawn from the low water mark of the South Coast of Pulau Merambong. At the Eastern entrance ... next through the centre of the
-- deep-water channel between Johore Shoal and the mainland of Johore, Southward of Johore Hill, and finally turning Southward, to
-- intersect the 3-mile limit drawn from the low water mark of the mainland of Johore in a position bearing 192 degrees from Tanjong
-- Sitapa."
GIVEN `the entrance` IS AN Entrance
GIVETH A `Seaward end`
DECIDE `where the boundary ends seaward` IS
    CONSIDER `the entrance`
    WHEN `the Western entrance` THEN `the 3-mile limit from the low water mark of the South Coast of Pulau Merambong`
    WHEN `the Eastern entrance` THEN `the 3-mile limit from the low water mark of the Johore mainland, bearing 192 degrees from Tanjong Sitapa`

-- "The boundary as so defined is approximately delineated in red on the map annexed hereunto ... Should, however, the map, owing to
-- alterations in the channels, etc., appear at any time to conflict with the text of this Agreement, the text shall in all cases
-- prevail." "etc." and "in all cases": the cause of the conflict does not matter.
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `Cause of conflict`
GIVETH AN Authority
DECIDE `what prevails where the map conflicts with the text` IS `the text of the Agreement`

§§ `Articles I and II -- whose territorial waters`

-- Article II: "Subject to the provisions of Article I hereof, all those waters ceded by Their Highnesses the Sultan and Tumungong of
-- Johore under Treaty of the 2nd of August 1824 which are within three nautical miles of the mainland of the State and Territory of
-- Johore measured from low water mark shall be deemed to be within the Territorial waters of the State and Territory of Johore."
--
-- "Subject to the provisions of Article I": inside Johore Strait the channel line governs, so water on the Singapore side of the line
-- stays the Settlement's even though (as the narrow Strait makes likely) it is within three miles of the Johore mainland.
-- INFERENCE: ceded water outside the Strait and beyond the three miles is not given to Johore by the Agreement, so it stays as the 1824
-- Treaty left it (the Settlement's). The Agreement does not say so in terms. Water never ceded in 1824 is outside the Agreement.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the Agreement is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Waters of`
DECIDE `whose territorial waters` IS
    IF NOT `the Agreement has force or effect` `the Agreement is approved`
    THEN `not decided by the Agreement`
    ELSE IF `the place`'s `in Johore Strait or at its entrances`
         THEN IF `the place`'s `on the Johore mainland side of the boundary line`
              THEN `the State and Territory of Johore`
              ELSE `the Settlement of Singapore`
         ELSE IF `the place`'s `among the waters ceded by the 1824 Treaty`
                   AND `the place`'s `within three nautical miles of the Johore mainland from low water mark`
              THEN `the State and Territory of Johore`
              ELSE IF `the place`'s `among the waters ceded by the 1824 Treaty`
                   THEN `the Settlement of Singapore`
                   ELSE `not decided by the Agreement`

§§ `Article III -- islets`

-- Article III: "All islets lying within the Territorial waters of the State and Territory of Johore, as defined in Articles I and II
-- hereof, which immediately prior to this Agreement formed part of His Britannic Majesty's dominions, are hereby ceded in full
-- sovereignty and property to His Highness the Sultan of the State and Territory of Johore, his heirs and successors for ever."
GIVEN `lies within Johore's territorial waters as defined` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `formed part of His Britannic Majesty's dominions immediately before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the islet is ceded to the Sultan of Johore` IF
    `lies within Johore's territorial waters as defined` AND `formed part of His Britannic Majesty's dominions immediately before`
